line	<str>With the rock and ball of wool in your inventory, use the ogre bellows on the bloated toad for a balloon toad.</str>
line	
line	<str>Drop the balloon toad and kill the Jubbly with ogre arrows. You may have to attempt multiple times.</str>
line	
line	<str>Cook the Jubbly on Rantz's spit-roast.</str>
line	
line	<str>Give the Cooked jubbly to Skrach Uglogwee in Lumbridge.</str>
line	
line	<str>Inspect Sir Amik.</str>
line	
line	<str>Ask the cook how you helped Sir Amik Varze.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use milk on cream.</str>
line	
line	<str>If you need a pot of cornflour, grind raw sweetcorn in a windmill and fill a pot with it.</str>
line	
line	<str>Add the pot of cornflour to the milky mixture.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pick a vanilla pod in the Kharazi Jungle (SW of the pool used in Legends' Quest), add it to the cornflour mixture.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to the Wise Old Man in Draynor, ask about strange beasts, then the Evil Chicken. Make sure you finish the dialogue or you will not be able to proceed.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use a raw chicken on the Evil Chicken shrine in northern Zanaris (where you arrive from the swamp.)</str>
line	
line	<str>Run north past the dragons and kill the Evil Chicken, pick up its egg and add it to the brulee.</str>
line	
line	<str>Kill a black dragon, there is a safespot to the east, pick up the dragon token.</str>
line	
line	<str>Grind a dramen branch with a pestle and mortar to make cinnamon, add it to the brulee.</str>
line	
line	<str>Return to Zanaris through the southern portal.</str>
line	
line	<str>Equip ice gloves then rub the token.</str>
line	
line	<str>Give the Brulee supreme to Sir Amik in Lumbridge.</str>
line	
line	<str>Inspect Awowogei.</str>
line	
line	<str>Travel to Ape Atoll, equip a monkey greegree and M'speak amulet.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Awowogei south of the temple.</str>
line	
line	<str>If you need a banana and monkey nuts, buy them from the food store now.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to any of the 3 monkeys in the north-west corner of the temple.</str>
line	
line	<col=000080>Use your Banana and Monkey nuts on any of them. (Ensure you use both your Banana and Monkey nuts on them or else the Tchiki nuts will not appear on the bush.)</col>
step	89	-	Quick guide step 89
line	<str>Speak to the Lumbridge Cook.</str>
line	
line	<str>Speak to him again with items in inventory.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the door behind the Cook and watch the cutscene.</str>
line	
line	<str>Inspect the dwarf.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go to the Rising Sun Inn in Falador and talk to Emily or Kaylee. Pay her (Ring of Charos(a) persuades her for free) to learn how to make Asgoldian ale.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use coins on your Asgarnian ales.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go to the tunnel under White Wolf Mountain.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to "An old Dwarf" (Rohak) and give him Asgoldian ales until he agrees to make a dwarven rock cake.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to him 3 times and he will place a dwarven rock cake on the table. (His name will change to Rohak)</str>
line	
line	<str>If you have ice gloves, equip them and pick up the cake. Otherwise pick up the cake with regular gloves then kill an icefiend (at Ice Mountain) to cool the cake. If you forgot to use the ice gloves, you can drop the cake, equip your ice gloves, and pick the cake back up to cool it.</str>
line	
line	<str>Give the dwarven rock cake to the dwarf in Lumbridge.</str>
line	
line	<str>Inspect one of the goblin generals.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go to the Goblin Village and climb down the ladder in the north-east building.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to the Goblin Cook (Mudknuckles). , then talk to him again and give him the charcoal.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to the Goblin Cook again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to the Goblin Cook again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Give the slop of compromise to the generals in Lumbridge.</str>
line	
line	<str>Inspect Pirate Pete.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to the cook in the next room about protecting the pirate.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go through all 5 chat options.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use your pestle and mortar on the raw cod.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use your knife on the bread and make breadcrumbs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Murphy in Port Khazard.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Murphy again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Equip your fishbowl helmet and diving apparatus, agree to go diving.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pick some kelp.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go north and talk to Nung.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go west and pick up 5 rocks, then enter the cave.</str>
line	
line	<str>Kill 5 mudskippers (level 30/31) for 5 hides.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Nung twice.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the crab pen, kill at least one crab and take its meat (acquire multiple in case the fishcake is burnt).</str>
line	
line	<str>Use your pestle and mortar to grind the kelp and crab meat.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to the Cook in Lumbridge about freeing the pirate again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the ingredients (ground cod, breadcrumbs, ground kelp and ground crab meat) on each other then cook the fishcake.</str>
line	
line	<str>Give the fishcake to Pirate Pete in Lumbridge.</str>
line	
line	<str>Inspect the Lumbridge Guide.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Wizard Traiborn on the uk=1 of the Wizards' Tower.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to him again to enchant the egg by identifying 3 mystery NPCs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to him again to enchant the milk by answering trivia.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to him a third time to enchant the flour with a memory test.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take a screenshot of the items and then close the interface via the X button to answer the questions.</str>
line	
line	<str>Do not use the ESC key to close the interface as it will reset that portion of the test!</str>
line	
line	<str>Use one of the ingredients on the cake tin, then cook the raw cake.</str>
line	
line	<str>Give the cake of guidance to the Lumbridge guide.</str>
line	
line	<str>Inspect Evil Dave</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Evil Dave in Edgeville (down the trapdoor).</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Doris upstairs.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use your cat to catch hell-rats (right-click chase on your cat). Using a fully grown cat is much more efficient, but using a kitten still works.</str>
line	
line	<str>Collect spices from hell-rats. There are 4 spices to collect: yellow, orange, red, brown. Collect at least 3 doses of each.</str>
line	
line	<str>Now find the perfectly spiced stew with the right quantity of all 4 colours of spice.</str>
line	
line	<str>Give Evil Dave the completed stew, then give him that spicy stew in Lumbridge.</str>
line	
line	<str>Inspect Skrach Uglogwee.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Rantz . (You can use the fairy ring code AKS and run east)</str>
line	
line	<str>Go south-east and talk to Rantz by the coast.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use your woodcutting axe on the fallen tree twice.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to him again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Get some raw chompies if needed.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go to Karamja and find the tree with an arrow in it (small tree on the coast, just south of transportation icon west of Tai Bwo Wannai).</str>
line	
line	<str>Light a fire next to the tree, use your iron spit on a raw chompy, then cook it.</str>
line	
line	<str>Board the ogre boat.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Rantz south-east near the coast.</str>
line	
line	<str>Collect a bloated toad from the nearby swamp.</str>
line	
line	<str>Make sure your ogre bellow has at least 1 charge remaining</str>
line	
line	<str>Get a rock from the mine by Rantz' cave.</str>
line	
line	<str>With the rock and ball of wool in your inventory, use the ogre bellows on the bloated toad for a balloon toad.</str>
line	
line	<str>Drop the balloon toad and kill the Jubbly with ogre arrows. You may have to attempt multiple times.</str>
line	
line	<str>Cook the Jubbly on Rantz's spit-roast.</str>
line	
line	<str>Give the Cooked jubbly to Skrach Uglogwee in Lumbridge.</str>
line	
line	<str>Inspect Sir Amik.</str>
line	
line	<str>Ask the cook how you helped Sir Amik Varze.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use milk on cream.</str>
line	
line	<str>If you need a pot of cornflour, grind raw sweetcorn in a windmill and fill a pot with it.</str>
line	
line	<str>Add the pot of cornflour to the milky mixture.</str>
line	
line	<str>Pick a vanilla pod in the Kharazi Jungle (SW of the pool used in Legends' Quest), add it to the cornflour mixture.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to the Wise Old Man in Draynor, ask about strange beasts, then the Evil Chicken. Make sure you finish the dialogue or you will not be able to proceed.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use a raw chicken on the Evil Chicken shrine in northern Zanaris (where you arrive from the swamp.)</str>
line	
line	<str>Run north past the dragons and kill the Evil Chicken, pick up its egg and add it to the brulee.</str>
line	
line	<str>Kill a black dragon, there is a safespot to the east, pick up the dragon token.</str>
line	
line	<str>Grind a dramen branch with a pestle and mortar to make cinnamon, add it to the brulee.</str>
line	
line	<str>Return to Zanaris through the southern portal.</str>
line	
line	<str>Equip ice gloves then rub the token.</str>
line	
line	<str>Give the Brulee supreme to Sir Amik in Lumbridge.</str>
line	
line	<str>Inspect Awowogei.</str>
line	
line	<str>Travel to Ape Atoll, equip a monkey greegree and M'speak amulet.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Awowogei south of the temple.</str>
line	
line	<str>If you need a banana and monkey nuts, buy them from the food store now.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to any of the 3 monkeys in the north-west corner of the temple.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use your Banana and Monkey nuts on any of them. (Ensure you use both your Banana and Monkey nuts on them or else the Tchiki nuts will not appear on the bush.)</str>
line	
line	<col=000080>If you already have a gorilla, ninja, and zombie monkey greegree then skip this part.</col>
