line	<str>If you already have a gorilla, ninja, and zombie monkey greegree then skip this part.</str>
line	
line	<str>Note: You should take at least 3 snake corpses, red bananas, and tchiki nuts in case you burn the stuffed snake (use the drop trick for the nuts and the banana).</str>
line	
line	<str>Travel to Crash Island and climb down the pit. Kill some level 84 big snakes for their corpses. (Recommended to pray melee before descending into the pit)</str>
line	
line	<str>Return to Ape Atoll and find the red banana tree north-west of the big gate (by the shore).</str>
line	
line	<str>Equip your gorilla greegree and use a rope on the tree to get some red bananas.</str>
line	
line	<str>Equip your ninja greegree and enter the Ape Atoll agility course.</str>
line	
line	<str>After swinging the rope, enter the hole and pick some tchiki nuts.</str>
line	
line	<str>Grind the tchiki nuts, slice the red banana, and add them to the snake corpses.</str>
line	
line	<str>Equip your zombie greegree and enter the temple dungeon.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go down one of the ramps and enter the crack in the wall between the two ramps.</str>
line	
line	<str>Lay your stuffed snake on the rock to cook it (requires 70 cooking).</str>
line	
line	<str>Give the cooked stuffed snake to Awowogei in Lumbridge.</str>
line	
line	<str>You will need 175 Quest Points and complete Desert Treasure I and Horror from the Deep before entering the portal.</str>
line	
line	<col=000080>Remember, you can bank between every kill. Enter the portal and defeat without prayers:</col>
done	<str>Speak to the Lumbridge Cook.</str>
done	
done	<str>Speak to him again with items in inventory.</str>
done	
done	<str>Enter the door behind the Cook and watch the cutscene.</str>
done	
done	<str>Inspect the dwarf.</str>
done	
done	<str>Go to the Rising Sun Inn in Falador and talk to Emily or Kaylee. Pay her (Ring of Charos(a) persuades her for free) to learn how to make Asgoldian ale.</str>
done	
done	<str>Use coins on your Asgarnian ales.</str>
done	
done	<str>Go to the tunnel under White Wolf Mountain.</str>
done	
done	<str>Talk to "An old Dwarf" (Rohak) and give him Asgoldian ales until he agrees to make a dwarven rock cake.</str>
done	
done	<str>Talk to him 3 times and he will place a dwarven rock cake on the table. (His name will change to Rohak)</str>
done	
done	<str>If you have ice gloves, equip them and pick up the cake. Otherwise pick up the cake with regular gloves then kill an icefiend (at Ice Mountain) to cool the cake. If you forgot to use the ice gloves, you can drop the cake, equip your ice gloves, and pick the cake back up to cool it.</str>
done	
done	<str>Give the dwarven rock cake to the dwarf in Lumbridge.</str>
done	
done	<str>Inspect one of the goblin generals.</str>
done	
done	<str>Go to the Goblin Village and climb down the ladder in the north-east building.</str>
done	
done	<str>Talk to the Goblin Cook (Mudknuckles). , then talk to him again and give him the charcoal.</str>
done	
done	<str>Talk to the Goblin Cook again.</str>
done	
done	<str>Talk to the Goblin Cook again.</str>
done	
done	<str>Give the slop of compromise to the generals in Lumbridge.</str>
done	
done	<str>Inspect Pirate Pete.</str>
done	
done	<str>Talk to the cook in the next room about protecting the pirate.</str>
done	
done	<str>Go through all 5 chat options.</str>
done	
done	<str>Use your pestle and mortar on the raw cod.</str>
done	
done	<str>Use your knife on the bread and make breadcrumbs.</str>
done	
done	<str>Talk to Murphy in Port Khazard.</str>
done	
done	<str>Talk to Murphy again.</str>
done	
done	<str>Equip your fishbowl helmet and diving apparatus, agree to go diving.</str>
done	
done	<str>Pick some kelp.</str>
done	
done	<str>Go north and talk to Nung.</str>
done	
done	<str>Go west and pick up 5 rocks, then enter the cave.</str>
done	
done	<str>Kill 5 mudskippers (level 30/31) for 5 hides.</str>
done	
done	<str>Talk to Nung twice.</str>
done	
done	<str>Enter the crab pen, kill at least one crab and take its meat (acquire multiple in case the fishcake is burnt).</str>
done	
done	<str>Use your pestle and mortar to grind the kelp and crab meat.</str>
done	
done	<str>Talk to the Cook in Lumbridge about freeing the pirate again.</str>
done	
done	<str>Use the ingredients (ground cod, breadcrumbs, ground kelp and ground crab meat) on each other then cook the fishcake.</str>
done	
done	<str>Give the fishcake to Pirate Pete in Lumbridge.</str>
done	
done	<str>Inspect the Lumbridge Guide.</str>
done	
done	<str>Talk to Wizard Traiborn on the uk=1 of the Wizards' Tower.</str>
done	
done	<str>Talk to him again to enchant the egg by identifying 3 mystery NPCs.</str>
done	
done	<str>Talk to him again to enchant the milk by answering trivia.</str>
done	
done	<str>Talk to him a third time to enchant the flour with a memory test.</str>
done	
done	<str>Take a screenshot of the items and then close the interface via the X button to answer the questions.</str>
done	
done	<str>Do not use the ESC key to close the interface as it will reset that portion of the test!</str>
done	
done	<str>Use one of the ingredients on the cake tin, then cook the raw cake.</str>
done	
done	<str>Give the cake of guidance to the Lumbridge guide.</str>
done	
done	<str>Inspect Evil Dave</str>
done	
done	<str>Talk to Evil Dave in Edgeville (down the trapdoor).</str>
done	
done	<str>Talk to Doris upstairs.</str>
done	
done	<str>Use your cat to catch hell-rats (right-click chase on your cat). Using a fully grown cat is much more efficient, but using a kitten still works.</str>
done	
done	<str>Collect spices from hell-rats. There are 4 spices to collect: yellow, orange, red, brown. Collect at least 3 doses of each.</str>
done	
done	<str>Now find the perfectly spiced stew with the right quantity of all 4 colours of spice.</str>
done	
done	<str>Give Evil Dave the completed stew, then give him that spicy stew in Lumbridge.</str>
done	
done	<str>Inspect Skrach Uglogwee.</str>
done	
done	<str>Talk to Rantz . (You can use the fairy ring code AKS and run east)</str>
done	
done	<str>Go south-east and talk to Rantz by the coast.</str>
done	
done	<str>Use your woodcutting axe on the fallen tree twice.</str>
done	
done	<str>Talk to him again.</str>
done	
done	<str>Get some raw chompies if needed.</str>
done	
done	<str>Go to Karamja and find the tree with an arrow in it (small tree on the coast, just south of transportation icon west of Tai Bwo Wannai).</str>
done	
done	<str>Light a fire next to the tree, use your iron spit on a raw chompy, then cook it.</str>
done	
done	<str>Board the ogre boat.</str>
done	
done	<str>Talk to Rantz south-east near the coast.</str>
done	
done	<str>Collect a bloated toad from the nearby swamp.</str>
done	
done	<str>Make sure your ogre bellow has at least 1 charge remaining</str>
done	
done	<str>Get a rock from the mine by Rantz' cave.</str>
done	
done	<str>With the rock and ball of wool in your inventory, use the ogre bellows on the bloated toad for a balloon toad.</str>
done	
done	<str>Drop the balloon toad and kill the Jubbly with ogre arrows. You may have to attempt multiple times.</str>
done	
done	<str>Cook the Jubbly on Rantz's spit-roast.</str>
done	
done	<str>Give the Cooked jubbly to Skrach Uglogwee in Lumbridge.</str>
done	
done	<str>Inspect Sir Amik.</str>
done	
done	<str>Ask the cook how you helped Sir Amik Varze.</str>
done	
done	<str>Use milk on cream.</str>
done	
done	<str>If you need a pot of cornflour, grind raw sweetcorn in a windmill and fill a pot with it.</str>
done	
done	<str>Add the pot of cornflour to the milky mixture.</str>
done	
done	<str>Pick a vanilla pod in the Kharazi Jungle (SW of the pool used in Legends' Quest), add it to the cornflour mixture.</str>
done	
done	<str>Talk to the Wise Old Man in Draynor, ask about strange beasts, then the Evil Chicken. Make sure you finish the dialogue or you will not be able to proceed.</str>
done	
done	<str>Use a raw chicken on the Evil Chicken shrine in northern Zanaris (where you arrive from the swamp.)</str>
done	
done	<str>Run north past the dragons and kill the Evil Chicken, pick up its egg and add it to the brulee.</str>
done	
done	<str>Kill a black dragon, there is a safespot to the east, pick up the dragon token.</str>
done	
done	<str>Grind a dramen branch with a pestle and mortar to make cinnamon, add it to the brulee.</str>
done	
done	<str>Return to Zanaris through the southern portal.</str>
done	
done	<str>Equip ice gloves then rub the token.</str>
done	
done	<str>Give the Brulee supreme to Sir Amik in Lumbridge.</str>
done	
done	<str>Inspect Awowogei.</str>
done	
done	<str>Travel to Ape Atoll, equip a monkey greegree and M'speak amulet.</str>
done	
done	<str>Talk to Awowogei south of the temple.</str>
done	
done	<str>If you need a banana and monkey nuts, buy them from the food store now.</str>
done	
done	<str>Talk to any of the 3 monkeys in the north-west corner of the temple.</str>
done	
done	<str>Use your Banana and Monkey nuts on any of them. (Ensure you use both your Banana and Monkey nuts on them or else the Tchiki nuts will not appear on the bush.)</str>
done	
done	<str>If you already have a gorilla, ninja, and zombie monkey greegree then skip this part.</str>
done	
done	<str>Note: You should take at least 3 snake corpses, red bananas, and tchiki nuts in case you burn the stuffed snake (use the drop trick for the nuts and the banana).</str>
done	
done	<str>Travel to Crash Island and climb down the pit. Kill some level 84 big snakes for their corpses. (Recommended to pray melee before descending into the pit)</str>
done	
done	<str>Return to Ape Atoll and find the red banana tree north-west of the big gate (by the shore).</str>
done	
done	<str>Equip your gorilla greegree and use a rope on the tree to get some red bananas.</str>
done	
done	<str>Equip your ninja greegree and enter the Ape Atoll agility course.</str>
done	
done	<str>After swinging the rope, enter the hole and pick some tchiki nuts.</str>
done	
done	<str>Grind the tchiki nuts, slice the red banana, and add them to the snake corpses.</str>
done	
done	<str>Equip your zombie greegree and enter the temple dungeon.</str>
done	
done	<str>Go down one of the ramps and enter the crack in the wall between the two ramps.</str>
done	
done	<str>Lay your stuffed snake on the rock to cook it (requires 70 cooking).</str>
done	
done	<str>Give the cooked stuffed snake to Awowogei in Lumbridge.</str>
done	
done	<str>You will need 175 Quest Points and complete Desert Treasure I and Horror from the Deep before entering the portal.</str>
done	
done	<str>Remember, you can bank between every kill. Enter the portal and defeat without prayers:</str>
done	
done	<col=ff0000>QUEST COMPLETE!</col>
